# A 1.x checkout kept WiFi credentials, the SK host and the wake word in
# platformio_local.ini. Nothing reads it any more, but an old working tree
# may still hold one, and it must never be staged.
platformio_local.ini

# dependencies.lock is COMMITTED, not ignored: this is an application, and an
# application pins its registry dependencies exactly through its lock so CI
# builds the same binary a developer just flashed. Without it the component
# manager re-resolves on every run and can build against a different component
# set than the one that was tested. espOS states the same rule for the same
# reason (espos/.gitignore); libraries use version ranges instead.
# Update deliberately with `idf.py update-dependencies` and commit the diff.

# Agent / tooling scratch
.claude/
.build/
cr-review-*

# Local capture + diagnostic artefacts. Mic probes (/mic_probe returns a
# WAV) and merged firmware images land here during on-hardware debugging;
# the merged image is a release asset built by CI, never a tracked file.
# Scoped rather than a blanket *.bin so a vendored component's binary can
# still be committed deliberately.
*.wav
/espos-p4-cockpit-merged*.bin
/cockpit-merged*.bin

# ---- espOS / ESP-IDF 6 project (branch espos) ----
build/
build-*/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
# Bench-local overrides espos_project_prologue() layers on top of sdkconfig.defaults.
sdkconfig.local
managed_components/
secure_boot_signing_key.pem
*.pem
*.nvs.csv
*.nvs.bin
provisioning/
secrets/

# Python bytecode from running scripts/*.py
__pycache__/
